<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berlin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Berlin-Cölln</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berlin is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It grew from medieval trading towns on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spree">Spree</a> into the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a> and, from 1871, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>. It hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> of 1878 and the Berlin Conference on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> of 1884–1885. Divided after 1945 and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a> from 1961 to 1989, it became the capital of reunited Germany in 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berlin.jpg" alt="Berlin" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Museumsinsel Berlin Juli 2021 1 (cropped).jpg: Kasa Fue derivative work: Georgfotoart · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museumsinsel_Berlin_Juli_2021_1_(cropped)_b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
